{
 "provenance": {
  "captured": "2026-10-12",
  "where": "the bench LAN: 224.0.0.251:5353 joined on 192.168.2.48, the same box orb-manager and orbfake run on",
  "by": "a raw UDP join with SO_REUSEADDR, held open while orb-manager's own browser read the same group",
  "who": "neighbour stacks only \u2014 a Chromecast, Home Assistant probes, an iPad's _companion-link/_services advertisement, printer and IoT announcements. Nothing from this repo: the two sockets this project owns were dropped from the sample",
  "why": "every packet here arrived unsolicited on a live subnet and is fed to the browser as noise. The browser must parse or ignore all of them and record NO refusal: a refusal over a well-formed neighbour packet is how a device nobody asked about fills the hub's card with our defect. Three shapes did refuse before they were fixed \u2014 the name walker read a record's TYPE from inside an expanded name (reserved label form 0x65, RDLENGTH 28525), and the TXT decoder refused RFC 6762's empty character-string and RFC 6763's flag string, which took the whole datagram with them."
 },
